// CROWN — a MIXED declared row on a HOF, `with F + !E`: the positive half
// licenses F for the body, and the negation half must still reach the
// parameter. Expect E_EffectMismatch.
//
// Checked clean and ran at 10 through the pinned boot (measured
// 2026-09-23): the declared-row fold collapses `F + !E` to the closed row
// {F}, so the negation never exists as a bound on anything.
effect F { fop() -> Int }
effect E { op() -> Int }
fn run(f) with F + !E = fop() + f()
fn bad() = run(() => op())
handler hf { fop() => resume(3) }
handler eh { op() => resume(7) }
fn main() = ((bad()) ~> hf) ~> eh
